> a/CHANGELOG.md +* Redact URL fragments containing sensitive parameters before DevTools stores URL headers or redirect locations. Harmless fragments and live redirect responses are unchanged (@thomasklemm)
> a/docs/guide/devtools.md +A URL fragment that carries a sensitive parameter, such as `#access_token=…` or a hash-router query, is replaced whole with `[REDACTED]`: fragment syntax is up to the app, so there is no safe way to cut out one value. Other fragments are stored as they are.
